n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558544 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a3f4d85-0623-5fd9-9cc9-8c8eac44c1ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558544 #edb/ref 1074 "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{3(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-s)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}(t-2){e}^{3(t-1)} \\\\ {e}^{3(t-1)}\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{1}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558563 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186558464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558563 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186558478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558563 #edb/ref 1069 "q-334859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558563 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558563 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWrite down the expression that gives the solution of the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">$\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td><td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}} </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,\\text{d}s$</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td><td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">${e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558563 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb2daa37-d9b1-570d-9a42-38ab64cc0e59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558563 #edb/ref 1074 "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At}\\,x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t)+2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]+{\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{s}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(t-s) \\\\ {e}^{s}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(t-s)\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558616 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186558657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186558616 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3cf553b5-a0c0-5e03-